  "raw_policy_excerpt": "#Amazon Vulnerability Research Program (VRP) - Program Policy\n\n#Rules of Engagement (Testing)\n- Use User-Agent string 'amazonvrpresearcher_yourh1username' while testing.\n- Limited usage of automated scanners/tools is allowed with the above User-Agent applied; scanners must be configured to not send more than 5 requests per second to any particular service.\n- Use of scanning tools without the User-Agent string may result in account/IP getting blocked by automated protections.\n- Do not use 3rd party sites when testing (e.g. XSS Hunter variants). Only utilize assets that you expressly own and control yourself.\n- When testing a subdomain takeover, do not publish anything on the index page. Serve an HTML file on a hidden path containing your HackerOne username in an HTML comment.\n- Create Amazon accounts using yourh1username@wearehackerone.com.\n\n#Always Out of Scope\n- Anything which contains 'aws' in the subdomain\n- Anything which is .a2z.\n- Anything which ends with *.dev\n- Anything which redirects to AWS\n- URLs with text: test, qa, integ, preprod, gamma, beta, user-aliases, regions (us-east, us-west)\n- AWS and AWS customer assets\n- Security issues in the AWS IP Space (https://ip-ranges.amazonaws.com/ip-ranges.json)\n\n#Legal Safe Harbor\nAmazon will not bring any legal action against anyone who makes a good faith effort to comply with program policies, or for any accidental or good faith violation of this policy.\n\n#Operational Security Issues\nOpSec issues (leaked employee passwords, leaked business documents, etc.) will only receive reputation points — no monetary reward.\n\n#Non-eligible Vulnerabilities\nClickjacking, Self XSS, Email Spoofing/SPF, Subdomain Takeover for out-of-scope items, Scanner Outputs, DOS/DDOS, Missing Cookie Flags, Content Spoofing, Stack Traces/Path Disclosure/Directory Listings, CSV Injection, Reflected File Download, Auth User Enumeration, Password Complexity, HTTP Trace Method, Host Header Injection without demonstrable impact, CSRF with minimal impact.\n\n#Bounty Eligibility Note\nBounty amounts are not published. offers_bounties=true per GraphQL. Program is open (submission_state=open)."
